<title>FRANCE: UAP nine-month sales flat.</title>
<headline>UAP nine-month sales flat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine-months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover				     114,081    vs  114,649</p>
<p>    UAP France				    48,681    vs  48,834</p>
<p>    UAP Central and Eastern Europe	  26,888    vs  25,744</p>
<p>    UAP Britain and Ireland		   14,963    vs  12,388</p>
<p>    UAP Benelux and northern Europe	 13,213    vs  13,227</p>
<p>    UAP International			    7,974    vs   7,364</p>
<p>    Scor						-	 vs   5,000</p>
<p>    Transversal activities		     2,362    vs   2,092</p>
<p>Note - Union des Assurances de Paris, which is to merge with rival insurer Axa, said the 0.5 percent decline in its turnover was due to the sale of a 30 percent stake in Scor as well as UAP Allgemeine and UAP Leben. On a like-for-like basis, turnover rose 3.9 percent. Life insurance sales rose 4.5 percent or 5.4 percent on a like-for-like basis as a result of strong growth in Britain and Ireland where sales rose 23.2 percent. In non-life, sales fell 4.4 percent because of the sale of the Scor stake but rose 2.6 percent on a like-for-like basis. The percentage of turnover achieved outside France was 62.6 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
